  	<activity>
	<title>Sensemaking Check</title>
	<introduction>
		<p>
			
		</p>
				<p>Consider the charge diagram below of a conductor in an external electric field.</p>
				<figure xml:id="conductor-img2">
			  <title>Charged Conductor Figure</title>
			<caption>A charged conductor and an external electric field.</caption>
			<image source="ConductorCharged.png" width = "75%" ><description>A circular gray conductor in an upward pointing electric field.  Positive charges line the top of the conductor and negative charges line the bottom.  Points A and B are separated vertically inside the circle.</description></image>
		</figure>
	</introduction>

		<task>
			<p>What direction is the net electric field at each point inside the conductor?  Explain your reasoning.</p>
		</task>
		<task>
			<p>Do you think the electric potential difference between points A and B is positive, negative, or zero?  Explain your reasoning.</p>
		</task>
	</activity>

